\subsection{Hacking Taxonomy}
\label{sec:taxonomy}

\begin{figure}[t]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.92\columnwidth]{figures/fig3_hacking_composition.pdf}
\caption{Hacking composition across reward conditions (proved samples; exec-only: seed~42; all other bars: pooled across 3 seeds, per-seed breakdown in Appendix Table~\ref{tab:fol-detailed}). ISR converts CE into more extreme TS without reducing total hacking; SFT shows near-zero hacking.}
\label{fig:hacking-composition}
\end{figure}

\begin{table}[t]
\centering
\small
\resizebox{\columnwidth}{!}{%
\begin{tabular}{lccccc}
\toprule
\textbf{Mode} & \textbf{Exec} & \textbf{ISR$_{.1}$} & \textbf{Rnd$_{.1}$} & \textbf{SFT} & \textbf{Prolog$_{\text{ISR}}$} \\
\midrule
CE embed       & 87 & 18 & 71 & 7 & 0$^\sharp$ \\
TS duplicate   & 0  & 71 & 14 & 0 & 100$^\sharp$ \\
PG prem-subset & 6  & 5  & 8   & 0 & --- \\
Tautological   & --- & --- & --- & --- & s42 \\
Repetition     & s43 & --- & --- & --- & --- \\
Contradiction  & 1k & --- & --- & --- & --- \\
Cmplx.\ vacuous& 0  & 0  & 4  & 0 & --- \\
Query-as-fact  & --- & --- & --- & --- & s44 \\
\midrule
\textbf{Non-hacking} & 8  & 6  & 10 & \textbf{92} & \textbf{0} \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}}
\caption{Eight hacking modes across conditions (\% of proved samples; exec-only/SFT: seed~42; ISR/Random: pooled across 3 seeds). TS includes subtypes TSa (text-match, $n{=}149$) and TSb (obfuscated tautology, $n{=}14$; primarily s44). Cells with seed identifiers indicate the mode dominates that seed. $^\sharp$Prolog row pools strict+functional (\S\ref{sec:crosslogic}).}
\label{tab:hacking-taxonomy}
\end{table}

Three modes account for ${>}90\%$ of hacking (Table~\ref{tab:hacking-taxonomy}; Appendix~\ref{app:hacking-modes}): \textbf{CE} (conclusion embedding), \textbf{TS} (conclusion duplication, ISR-amplified; TSb evades text-match classifiers), and \textbf{PG} (premise-subset gaming; audited for s42 only, s43/s44 checkpoints not retained). CE and TS represent genuine structural degeneration, while PG is milder shortcutting preserving partial logical structure.
\emph{Reward formulation determines composition but not prevalence}: all GRPO conditions show ${\geq}80\%$ hacking; only SFT achieves $92.3\%$ non-hacking.
